                        "review": "TL;DR feels like a completely different game, and I'm loving it!\r\n\r\nWot I liked\r\n- All systems got a major rehaul;\r\n- Reasonable numbers in damage and health;\r\n- A very fresh idea that you can main one strategy faction and choose between them when you start a strategy map;\r\n- Factions are more different than in the previous parts;\r\n- Journeymode - fun extra adventuring through several special scenarios with a custom party;\r\n- The dialogues are great: a very nice story, your companions have their own backgrounds and quests and addition unlockable perks and they also chime in in conversations;\r\n- AI is much better - they do different comps, attack different points - create a lot of distress and hate;\r\n- Great adventuring structure: you are neither hand-held nor forced to explore - you can turn down or skip a lot of stuff;\r\n- Good storytelling. I was doing a quest, made my choice, then my NPC told me to follow his orders because he outranked me;\r\n- Radial menues!\r\n- New engine/graphics, game's visuals are on a different level, even though it was released only 4 years after the last sf2 expac;\r\n- At the long last they allow us to change controls;\r\n- Limited Tactical pause at last;\r\n- Party size limit - 4 guys are less unmanageable than 8+;\r\n- More tactical options;\r\n- Yria is a darling;\r\n- The game has a bunch of in-game cutscenes and interactions that don't feel forced and enhance immersion;\r\n- Detailed game mechanics: different target types, statuses, condition, damage and armour types;\r\n- Indirect control over base management;\r\n- Menues in general are informative, detailed and customizeable. The gameguide is informative too;\r\n- Picturesque multilevel maps.\r\n\r\nWot I disliked\r\n- Only 12 shortcut bar for your whole team (and an additional bar) - too little;\r\n- Tactical combat is superfun, but with no pause you cannot really implement most of your stratagems;\r\n- If you don't bring heavy aoe to strategy sections you're dead meat;\r\n- Some settings do nothing;\r\n- Journeymode does not have save feature, so you might lose the map and waste quite a lot of time. Fail condition - your heroes die and the mission is failed: so you forgot about your guys for 10 seconds, they get killed, and you lose 2 hours of gametime - resplendid;\r\n- Journeymode has no accessories merchant;\r\n- Journeymode require internet connection even for single play. Lose connection? Bye-bye progress;\r\n- Journeymode has crafting only for trolls;\r\n- You can't create your full custom team in Journeymode;\r\n- You cannot freely move back and forth between maps;\r\n- Journeymode has flying creatures: you heroes do not have ranged weapons by default - switching weapons adds unnesessary additional micro;\r\n- The location of the blueprints and legendary item pieces is not so clear: I usually vacuum 99% of the stuff but here I missed like third of the different interesting stuff;\r\n- Big brawls are still a mess: I assume that the game is too fast for regular folks to micro macro and manage heroes at the same time;\r\n- Game is much more unmanageable in the beginning when your team is weak and you have neither items nor abilities, later your team acts as the fire brigade running from point to point deflecting\r\n- Limited number of resepec potions (in campaign): respeccing is fun. Maybe it'd be limited by only allowing to respec between missions or smth;\t\r\n- Many strategy missions just put you under a constant stream of enemies with no respite for hours;\r\n- Passive and active mode are something. Passive mode: your units dont move and only attack adjaacent targets. You turn this option on and your army is dead. Active mode: your units see the enemy in their base and go die under towers. Both these modes are horrible in a superfast game where AI keeps 30+ units on the map and you don't have time to micro because you are a normal human being;\r\n- In the beginning of the game every minute enemy drops swarms of enemies and the game is too bloody fast and your heroes are too weak - it's a big challenge;\r\n- I'm sad there's no game speed option and the pause they gave us is limited, tedious and slows down combat - I want a full RTwP!\r\n\r\nTo sum it all up, Spellforce 3 is a total overhaul of the series that has few connections to the previous titles, except for the general lore and universe. Nevertheless it is superfun experience that I immensely enjoyed. Give us RTwP!",
